## 7. CI / Release

### 7.1 Workflow `release-windows.yml`

```yaml
on:
  push:
    tags: ["v*"]
jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: windows-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable
        with: { targets: x86_64-pc-windows-msvc }
      - uses: pnpm/action-setup@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with: { node-version: 20, cache: pnpm }
      - run: pnpm -C apps/hoard-windows install --frozen-lockfile
      - run: pnpm -C apps/hoard-windows tauri build
        env:
          TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY: ${{ secrets.TAURI_KEY }}
          TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.TAURI_KEY_PWD }}
      - uses: softprops/action-gh-release@v2
        with:
          files: |
            apps/hoard-windows/src-tauri/target/release/bundle/msi/*.msi
            apps/hoard-windows/src-tauri/target/release/bundle/nsis/*.exe
            apps/hoard-windows/src-tauri/target/release/bundle/msi/*.msi.sig
```

### 7.2 Auto-update

- Tauri updater consume `latest.json` publicado como release asset:
  ```json
  {
    "version": "0.3.0",
    "notes": "...",
    "pub_date": "...",
    "platforms": {
      "windows-x86_64": {
        "signature": "...",
        "url": "https://github.com/rleeon/hoard/releases/download/v0.3.0/Hoard_0.3.0_x64-setup.nsis.zip"
      }
    }
  }
  ```
- Generar `latest.json` en el job de release (script bash post-build).

### 7.3 Code signing

- 0.3 sale **sin** code signing (cert EV ~$300/año). NSIS produce un instalador que dispara SmartScreen el primer mes; aceptar.
- Documentar pasos de "Run anyway" en `docs/install-windows.md`.
- Roadmap 0.4: comprar cert o usar Azure Trusted Signing.

